        li { margin-bottom: 5px; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Hari HRMS - Enterprise System Documentation</h1><br/><h2>1. System Overview</h2> <strong>Hari HRMS</strong> (Human Resource Management System) is a state-of-the-art, web-based platform designed to automate and streamline comprehensive HR operations. Built for scalability and high-fidelity user interaction, it bridges the gap between administrative efficiency and employee engagement.<br/><h3>Core Value Propositions (USPs)</h3> <ul><li>  <strong>Premium Aesthetics</strong>: Modern interface with glassmorphism, tailored HSL color palettes, and seamless dark mode synchronization.</li><li>  <strong>Native Collaboration</strong>: Integrated real-time messenger replacing third-party communication tools.</li><li>  <strong>Employee-Centric Design</strong>: morale-boosting features like the "Thursday Fun Chatbot" and automated celebration cards.</li><li>  <strong>Financial Precision</strong>: High-fidelity payroll processing with professional payslip generation and compliance-ready reports.</li></ul><br/>---<br/><h2>2. Technical Architecture</h2> The system follows a standard MERN stack architecture with real-time capabilities via WebSockets.<br/>| Layer | Technology | | :--- | :--- | | <strong>Frontend</strong> | React (Vite), Vanilla CSS, Framer Motion (Animations) | | <strong>Backend</strong> | Node.js, Express.js | | <strong>Database</strong> | MongoDB (Mongoose ODM) | | <strong>Real-time</strong> | Socket.io (Messenger & Notifications) | | <strong>Storage</strong> | Local Filesystem / Cloudinary (for uploads) | | <strong>Deployment</strong>| Vercel (Frontend/Backend) |<br/><h3>Backend Sub-structures</h3> <ul><li>  <strong>Controllers</strong>: Logic for handling API requests.</li><li>  <strong>Models</strong>: Data schemas and business rules.</li><li>  <strong>Services</strong>: Reusable modules (Email, Socket, Zoom Integration).</li><li>  <strong>Middleware</strong>: Security (JWT), Role-based Access Control (RBAC), File Uploads.</li></ul><br/>---<br/><h2>3. Functional Modules</h2><br/><h3>3.1 Employee Life-Cycle Management</h3> <ul><li>  <strong>Directory</strong>: Centralized repository for all staff records, searchable by department, role, or ID.</li><li>  <strong>Profile Management</strong>: Employee self-service for updating personal data, banking details, and profile images.</li><li>  <strong>Exit Management</strong>: Formal resignation workflow including reason tracking and clearance status.</li></ul><br/><h3>3.2 Time & Attendance</h3> A robust tracking system that handles complex shift patterns. <ul><li>  <strong>Clock-In/Out Logic</strong>:</li></ul>     *   <strong>Grace Period</strong>: Configurable window (default 15 mins) before status changes to 'Late'.     *   <strong>Night Shifts</strong>: Algorithmically handles sessions crossing midnight.     *   <strong>Half-Day Detection</strong>: Automatically flags based on actual hours worked (configurable, e.g., < 4 hrs). <ul><li>  <strong>Visual Calendar</strong>: Color-coded month view for employees to monitor their attendance history.</li></ul><br/><h3>3.3 Leave Management Workflow</h3> 1.  <strong>Application</strong>: Employee submits request with dates and reason. 2.  <strong>Validation</strong>: System checks for overlapping leaves and sufficient balance in real-time. 3.  <strong>Approval</strong>: HR/Managers receive email notifications and approve/reject via the dashboard. 4.  <strong>Auto-Deduction</strong>: Approved leaves are automatically deducted from the relevant balance (Casual, Sick, Earned).<br/><h3>3.4 Payroll & Finance</h3> The system automates the disbursement of salaries through professional workflows. <ul><li>  <strong>Calculations</strong>:</li></ul>     *   <strong>Earnings</strong>: Basic + DA + OA + Leave Wages.     *   <strong>Deductions</strong>: PF (Provident Fund), ESI, Professional Tax (PT), Labor Welfare Fund (LWF), TDS. <ul><li>  <strong>Features</strong>:</li></ul>     *   <strong>Bulk Processing</strong>: Import payroll data via Excel templates.     *   <strong>Disbursement</strong>: One-click "Mark as Paid" sends automated emails with salary credit notifications.     *   <strong>Analytics</strong>: Monthly and annual expenditure trends for management.<br/><h3>3.5 Internal Communications (Native Messenger)</h3> <ul><li>  <strong>11-on-1 & Group Chats</strong>: Persistent messaging with support for images and documents.</li><li>  <strong>Presence Status</strong>: Real-time "online/offline" indicators.</li><li>  <strong>Push Notifications</strong>: System-wide alerts for new messages, leave updates, and announcements.</li></ul><br/><h3>3.6 IT Support & Helpdesk</h3> <ul><li>  <strong>Ticketing System</strong>: Employees raise tickets for hardware, software, or HR issues.</li><li>  <strong>Central Tracking</strong>: HR/Admin view and resolve tickets, categorized by priority and status.</li></ul><br/>---<br/><h2>4. Operational Logic & System Governance</h2><br/><h3>4.1 Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)</h3> | Role | Capabilities | | :--- | :--- | | <strong>Admin</strong> | Full system control, settings configuration, audit logs, payroll formulas. | | <strong>HR Manager</strong> | Employee management, payroll processing, leave approvals, analytics. | | <strong>HR Assistant</strong> | Attendance tracking, ticket management, announcements. | | <strong>Employee</strong> | Self-dashboard, attendance history, leave application, payslip access. |<br/><h3>4.2 Automated Scheduled Jobs (Cron)</h3> <ul><li>  <strong>Fun Chatbot Cleanup</strong>: Every Sunday at midnight, the system automatically flushes the "Thursday Fun" submissions to maintain a fresh environment for the coming week.</li><li>  <strong>Birthday/Anniversary Scanning</strong>: Automated cards generated for employees celebrating milestones.</li></ul><br/><h3>4.3 Policy Configuration</h3> The <code>Setting</code> model governs the logic for the entire organization: <ul><li>  <strong>Leave Quotas</strong>: Annual limits for different leave types.</li><li>  <strong>Payroll Formulas</strong>: Wage ceilings for PF/ESI calculations and state-specific PT slabs.</li><li>  <strong>Company Branding</strong>: Office timings, logos, and communication signatures.</li></ul><br/>---<br/><h2>5. Security & Data Integrity</h2> <ul><li>  <strong>Authentication</strong>: JWT (JSON Web Tokens) with refresh token rotation.</li><li>  <strong>Encryption</strong>: Passwords hashed via Bcrypt; sensitive Zoom keys stored in environment variables.</li><li>  <strong>Validation</strong>: Server-side Mongoose schemas ensure data type consistency and required fields.</li><li>  <strong>Audit Logging</strong>: Every sensitive action (creation/deletion/payroll change) is logged with a timestamp and performing user ID.</li></ul><br/>--- <em>Generated for Stakeholders & Product Teams | © 2026 Hari HRMS</em> 
</body>
</html>
